1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,499
The outside pressure arrived at midday on a rainy afternoon, when an overseas advisor and an astronomer came to the backyard with a list.

2
00:00:08,499 --> 00:00:16,067
“You will modernize the station or we will place an intermediary from the capital,” the advisor said.

3
00:00:16,067 --> 00:00:24,806
“The chairperson wants the same view from every bank.” Patience was thinner than the fur on a camel.

4
00:00:24,806 --> 00:00:30,145
The respondent at the meeting was a teenager who kept a listener's notebook.

5
00:00:30,145 --> 00:00:35,399
“The bowel of this valley does not need a new garment,” she said.

6
00:00:35,399 --> 00:00:46,972
“It needs a mend.” A delightful gardening programme, an entertaining film, and an enjoyable concert had all been offered instead.

7
00:00:46,972 --> 00:00:56,145
The pressure was to enlarge, tighten, and harden: more concrete, more cages, more instrumentation.

8
00:00:56,145 --> 00:01:00,495
“Loosen the rules instead,” the carpenter said.

9
00:01:00,495 --> 00:01:13,308
“A garment that is too stiff will not clothe a growing child.” The electrician, the guitarist, the violinist, and the landlady all signed the same page.

10
00:01:13,308 --> 00:01:22,111
The danger was that the data would deteriorate if the budget were cut, or that the plan would materialize only as a monument.

11
00:01:22,111 --> 00:01:27,640
“Do not scold the volunteers for a slow week,” the boatman said.

12
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:36,724
“Solidify the method and let the numbers modernise themselves.” The noon reading had been missed twice.

13
00:01:36,724 --> 00:01:44,348
The counter-pressure was a raincoat, a pair of boots, and a chairperson who was willing to wait.

14
00:01:44,348 --> 00:01:54,531
“A pleasing report is not a persuasive one,” the advisor admitted, and the Celsius readings began to make sense to him.

15
00:01:54,531 --> 00:02:03,335
The condition imposed was simple and hard: three years of readings, published, before any construction.

16
00:02:03,335 --> 00:02:13,298
The group accepted the term, the west floor of the station became the archive, and the afternoon ended with a full set of signatures.

17
00:02:13,298 --> 00:02:18,827
The air was clear at noon, and the combat over the budget was not.

18
00:02:18,827 --> 00:02:33,019
A listener at the back asked madam chairperson to stiffen the rule rather than the concrete; nothing in the process would go into the story without the water readings, and the view from the well had to include us.

19
00:02:33,019 --> 00:02:41,803
The same set of instruments reached the same result twice, and the music from the guitarist covered the noise of the drills.

20
00:02:41,803 --> 00:02:50,035
The advisor would provide the list, put the money on the table, and start the clock.
